The full test suite is green: **280 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.

## Summary

I implemented the daily owner-registration limit in the owner creation endpoint.

**`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** (`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`) — after the existing duplicate/conflict checks, it now rejects with **400 Bad Request** when the daily limit is reached:

```java
if (dailyRegistrationLimitReached()) {
    return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);
}
```

The new helper counts stored owners whose `registrationDate` equals today and returns `true` once 20 exist:

```java
private static final long MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY = 20;

private boolean dailyRegistrationLimitReached() {
    LocalDate today = LocalDate.now();
    long registeredToday = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
        .filter(existing -> today.equals(existing.getRegistrationDate()))
        .count();
    return registeredToday >= MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY;
}
```

This is the only endpoint that creates owners (the V2 controller is read-only). Since new owners default their `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when unset, the 20th creation succeeds and the 21st for the day is rejected. Seed owners carry no registration date, so they never count toward the limit.

**Test added** — `createOwnerRejectedWhenDailyLimitReached` seeds 20 owners registered today and asserts the next POST returns 400.

